#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:3
msgid "Accessing your files using the Nextcloud web interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:5
msgid "You can access your Nextcloud files with the Nextcloud Web interface and create, preview, edit, delete, share, and re-share files. Your Nextcloud administrator has the option to disable these features, so if any of them are missing on your system ask your server administrator."
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:10
msgid "The Files app showing a list of files and folders."
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:14
msgid "Navigating your files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:16
msgid "The left sidebar lets you switch between different views of your files. Click a folder name in the file list to open it, and use your browser's back button or the breadcrumb bar at the top of the file list to return to a previous level."
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:20
msgid "The Files app left navigation panel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:23
msgid "The sidebar contains the following entries:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:25
msgid "All files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:26
msgid "The default view, showing every file and folder you have access to."
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:28
msgid "Recent"
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:29
msgid "Files you have viewed or modified recently."
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:31
msgid "Favorites"
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:32
msgid "Files and folders you have starred."
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:34
msgid "Shares"
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:35
msgid "Files shared with you, by you, or via a public link — all in one view."
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:37
msgid "Tags"
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:38
msgid "Browse files by system tag. See :doc:`tagging` for details on assigning tags and filtering your files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:41
msgid "Deleted files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:42
msgid "Files you have deleted that are still recoverable from the trash bin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:44
msgid "When you navigate into a folder, a breadcrumb trail appears at the top of the file list so you can jump back to any parent folder with a single click:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:47
msgid "Breadcrumb navigation inside a subfolder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:51
msgid "File controls"
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:53
msgid "Nextcloud displays thumbnail previews for images, text files, and other supported types — the exact list depends on your server configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:56
msgid "Each file and folder row has a three-dot action menu button. Click it to rename, move, copy, download, delete, or mark the item as a favorite. Files that have been marked as a favorite display a star icon:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:60
msgid "A file row with the actions menu open."
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:63
msgid "You can quickly find all your favorites using the **Favorites** entry in the left sidebar."
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:67
msgid "Details sidebar"
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:69
msgid "Select **Details** from the three-dot action menu to open the details sidebar. The sidebar shows information about the selected file and provides tabbed access to its activity history, sharing options, and version history:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:73
msgid "The details sidebar showing file information and tabs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:77
msgid "Activity and comments"
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:79
msgid "The **Activity** tab in the details sidebar shows a chronological log of changes to the file — uploads, edits, shares, and comments. You can leave a comment directly in this tab; comments are visible to everyone who has access to the file:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:84
msgid "The Activity tab showing file history and a comment field."
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:88
msgid "Searching and filtering"
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:90
msgid "Use the search bar at the top of the page to find files by name across all your files, or type in the search field inside the left sidebar to filter the current view:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:94
msgid "The search field with a search term entered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:98
msgid "Grid view"
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:100
msgid "The Files app defaults to a list view. Click the grid toggle button above the file list to switch to a thumbnail grid, which is useful for browsing image folders:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:104
msgid "Files displayed in thumbnail grid view."
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:107
msgid "Click the button again to return to the list view."
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:110
msgid "Uploading and creating files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:112
msgid "Click the **+** button near the top of the file list to upload files from your computer or create new items in the current folder:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:115
msgid "The New file and upload menu."
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:118
msgid "The menu offers the following options:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:120
msgid "Upload file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:121
msgid "Opens a file picker to upload one or more files from your computer. You can also drag and drop files directly from your file manager onto the file list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:124
msgid "Upload folder"
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:125
msgid "Uploads an entire folder, preserving its structure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:127
msgid "New folder"
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:128
msgid "Creates a new empty folder in the current location."
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:130
msgid "New document / New spreadsheet / New presentation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:131
msgid "Creates a new file using the built-in Nextcloud Text or Office editor, if enabled by your administrator."
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:135
msgid "Selecting files or folders"
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:137
msgid "Click the checkbox to the left of a file or folder to select it. To select all items in the current folder, click the checkbox in the column header."
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:140
msgid "With one or more items selected, action buttons appear at the top of the list. You can delete or download all selected items at once. Downloading multiple items produces a ZIP archive."
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:144
msgid "Multiple files selected with the bulk action bar visible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:147
msgid "If the **Download** button is not visible, your administrator has disabled this feature."
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:151
msgid "Sharing status icons"
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:153
msgid "Folders and files that have been shared display a **Shared** badge on their thumbnail or icon. Items shared via a public link also show a chain-link icon. Items that are not shared have no additional indicator."
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:157
msgid "File list showing a shared folder, a public-link-shared file, and unshared items."
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:160
msgid "See :doc:`sharing` for instructions on creating and managing shares."
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:163
msgid "Moving files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:165
msgid "Drag any file or folder and drop it onto a destination folder to move it. You can also use **Move or copy** from the three-dot action menu to move or copy items to a folder you choose from a picker dialog."
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:170
msgid "Previewing files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:172
msgid "Click a file name to open a preview directly in Nextcloud. Supported formats include images, plain text, PDF, and — depending on your server — office documents and audio files. If Nextcloud cannot preview a file format, it downloads the file to your computer instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:178
msgid "Video player"
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:180
msgid "You can play videos directly in Nextcloud by clicking the file. Playback depends on your browser and the video codec. See `MDN: Supported media formats <https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Supported_media_formats#Browser_compatibility>`_ for a compatibility reference."
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:186
msgid "Connecting to a Federation Share"
msgstr ""

#: ../../files/access_webgui.rst:188
msgid "Federated Cloud Sharing lets you mount file shares from remote Nextcloud servers and manage them just like local shares. See :doc:`federated_cloud_sharing` to learn how to create and connect to Federated Cloud shares."
msgstr ""
